@startuml SQ-04
title SQ-04 Pre-launch & Launch [P — launch semantics TBD: OQ-GP-01/02/19]
participant "Competitor Clients" as C
participant "Spectator Clients" as S
participant "Match Server" as MS
participant "Backend API" as B
MS -> MS : all competitors connected\nOR join timeout (P: 15 s, rule TBD OQ-GP-06)
MS -> B : MatchStateChanged {PRE_LAUNCH, present[], absent[]}
MS -> C : S2C_PhaseChanged {PRE_LAUNCH, startsAtServerTime, durationMs: 5000}
MS -> S : S2C_PhaseChanged {PRE_LAUNCH, ...}
note over C,MS
  **TBD** whether the 5 s is a countdown, the press window, or both.
  Mechanism proposed regardless of final rule:
  - client sends raw input events with client tick + sequence
  - server accepts only inside its own window (server clock)
  - server applies rate cap & formula from content data (FR-020)
end note
loop during accepted window
  C -> MS : C2S_LaunchInput {seq, kind: PRESS, clientTimeMs}
  MS -> MS : validate role=COMPETITOR, phase, rate cap (SEC-013/014)
end
MS -> MS : compute initialSpin = f(inputs, topStats)\n[formula TBD; data-driven]
MS -> C : S2C_PhaseChanged {BATTLE, launchResults[{userId, spinRate}]}
MS -> S : S2C_PhaseChanged {BATTLE, ...}
MS -> B : MatchStateChanged {BATTLE}
loop every snapshot interval (P: 20–30 Hz)
  MS -> C : S2C_Snapshot {tick, tops[]} (unreliable)
  MS -> S : S2C_Snapshot
end
@enduml
